        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9146-1",
        "name": "USN-9146-1",
        "description": "Joshua Rogers discovered that Privoxy incorrectly handled memory allocation, leading to a memory leak. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Privoxy to consume excessive resources, leading to a denial of service. (CVE-2021-44540)  Artem Ivanov discovered that Privoxy did not properly encode template names in error pages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to perform cross-site scripting attacks. (CVE-2021-44543)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2021-44540",
          "CVE-2021-44543"
        ]
      },
